@startuml component-oai-pmh
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: a new app apps/oai serves OAI-PMH 2.0 at /oai from its own table of
'       harvestable records (oai_records), never from live Entry queries; the
'       table is kept in step by OaiRecordSync, which re-projects an entry after
'       every relevant change and bumps the datestamp only when the projected
'       record's fingerprint changes, so opening a book never re-sends it.
' Kind: UML component diagram, specification level, proposal (IP-033).
'       Left: the read path (harvest). Right: the write path (sync).
'       Omitted: tracing, rate limits, the Dataverse app (unchanged).
' Source: OAI-PMH 2.0 spec + guidelines (openarchives.org, read 2026-11-16);
'         apps/core/models/entry.py, apps/core/touch.py, apps/content/citation.py,
'         knowledge ansible/roles/nginx/files/sites/evilflowers.elvira.stuba.sk
'         (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title OAI-PMH data provider: one view, one record table, one sync (proposal IP-033, 2026-11-16)

actor "Harvester\n(STU discovery, BASE)" as harvester
actor "Librarian · portal ·\nMCP · Dataverse sync" as editor

component "OaiPmhView · GET, POST /oai\nanonymous · text/xml\nRequestParser: verb grammar" as view <<proposed>>
component "OaiRepository\nsix verbs · OAI errors\nsigned stateless tokens" as repo <<proposed>> <<focus>>
component "Crosswalks\noai_dc · marc21" as crosswalks <<proposed>>

database "oai_records\nprojection · setSpecs ·\ndatestamp · deleted" as records <<proposed>>

database "core tables\nEntry · Catalog · Category ·\nAuthor · Acquisition" as core
component "Signal receivers\npost_save · post_delete ·\nm2m_changed" as receivers <<proposed>>
queue "Celery\nqueue default" as celery
component "Beat\noai.reconcile nightly" as beat <<proposed>>
component "OaiRecordSync\nsync(entry_ids) · reconcile()" as sync <<proposed>>
component "Projector + exposure rule\nEntry → RecordProjection,\nsetSpecs, exposed?" as projector <<proposed>>

' ---- layout only ------------------------------------------------------------------
harvester -[hidden]right- editor
crosswalks -[hidden]right- records

' ---- read path ----------------------------------------------------------------------
harvester -[$accent()]down-> view : <b>HTTPS ?verb=ListRecords</b>
view -[$accent()]down-> repo : <b>handle(OaiRequest)</b>
repo -[$accent()]down-> records : <b>keyset (datestamp, id)</b>
repo -down-> crosswalks : render(projection)

' ---- write path ---------------------------------------------------------------------
editor -down-> core : save · delete
core ..> receivers : signals
receivers -down-> celery : on commit:\noai.sync(ids)
celery -down-> sync : run task
beat -left-> sync : reconcile()
sync -down-> projector : project(entry)
projector -up-> core : read
sync -left-> records : upsert if fingerprint\nchanged · tombstone

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid box | exists in the catalog today |
  | dashed box, «proposed» | new in IP-033 |
  | blue fill, «focus» | the component this figure is about |
  | solid arrow | uses / calls, labelled with the operation |
  | dashed arrow | Django signal (notification) |
  | blue arrows | one harvest request |
endlegend

caption Harvesters read only oai_records: a stored projection per entry with setSpecs and a whole-second datestamp, tombstones included.\nOaiRecordSync re-projects an entry after a change (signals on entries, authors, categories, files, catalogs; on commit) and nightly\n(reconcile catches QuerySet.update() and bulk changes, which fire no signal); the datestamp moves only when the projection's fingerprint\nchanges. /oai needs no gateway change.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/component-oai-pmh.puml
@enduml
